        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "0038713c-bc12-368b-8759-18a29e7c9169",
                "word": "quetzal",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "3d0dd3be-307c-4202-a714-04bb74013ee4",
                        "entry_id": "0038713c-bc12-368b-8759-18a29e7c9169",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "quetzals"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "da844f5d-35a6-363e-aade-26935c9ad4ab",
                        "entry_id": "0038713c-bc12-368b-8759-18a29e7c9169",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Nom normalisé donné à deux genres comprenant six espèces d'oiseaux arboricoles de la famille des trogonidés, de taille supérieure à celle des trogons, au plumage principalement coloré de vert et de rouge, typiquement dotées de très longues rectrices ornementales, et fréquentant pour la plupart les forêts montagneuses de l'écozone néotropicale (genres Euptilotis et Pharomachrus)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2df5af40-96cb-41d3-9a64-e68ee89a7a36",
                                "sense_id": "da844f5d-35a6-363e-aade-26935c9ad4ab",
                                "text": "Ce fut le quetzal à longue queue, le plus beau de tous les oiseaux en terre maya, qui parla le premier : « Je vous en prie, servez-vous », offrit-il en tendant ses splendides plumes vertes."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d00fd7ad-0e2b-4018-9904-9bd7db4dc9e2",
                                "sense_id": "da844f5d-35a6-363e-aade-26935c9ad4ab",
                                "text": "Les quetzals sont présents uniquement en Amérique centrale. On en trouve dans la Sierra Madre au sud du Mexique (réserve de la biosphère El Triunfo), au Guatemala (réserve de la Sierra de Las Minas), au Honduras dans certaines petites réserves, au Nicaragua et enfin au Costa Rica […]."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5175c828-9065-32b6-ae25-1bf2e115cd71",
                        "entry_id": "0038713c-bc12-368b-8759-18a29e7c9169",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Monnaie du Guatemala."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4d437a13-cb50-4144-b89b-b8292b2d74de",
                                "sense_id": "5175c828-9065-32b6-ae25-1bf2e115cd71",
                                "text": "Nous extrayons de ce document les renseignements ci-dessous sur la situation économique du pays : Les moyens de payement se sont élevés en 1939 à la somme de 18.049.518 quetzals, chiffre qui est en augmentation de 1.878.098 quetzals sur celui de 1938, […]."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d76f99bf-7af2-4698-b048-5c150966abc2",
                                "sense_id": "5175c828-9065-32b6-ae25-1bf2e115cd71",
                                "text": "En 1921, un triumvirat dirigé par le général José Maria Orellana (1921-1926) renversa Herrera. Orellana entreprit de renégocier avec l'entreprise d'électricité Bond & Share ; il créa le quetzal comme monnaie en parité avec le dollar, ce qui était une dévaluation de fait, au bénéfice des producteurs de café."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3fb3dd88-9eb9-4eb6-b8cf-d0c074f3e7b6",
                        "source_entry_id": "0038713c-bc12-368b-8759-18a29e7c9169",
                        "source_sense_description": "oiseau",
                        "target_lang_word": "quetzal",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "quetzal",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6d651a00-ad1e-3d03-8f49-aec89d6754ff",
                                        "entry_id": "454ea17c-26aa-3d82-ab46-a6b20b839381",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any trogon of the genus Pharomacrus, especially a resplendent quetzal (Pharomacrus mocinno), which has very long tail feathers and is found in Guatemala and Costa Rica."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "05506556-f638-4129-a04f-834067f2a638",
                                                "sense_id": "6d651a00-ad1e-3d03-8f49-aec89d6754ff",
                                                "text": "Included among the images that Rigoberta Menchú uses in order to subtly convey her people's ethnicity is an image of Guatemala as the \"land of the quetzal.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bcddbdfb-ed8a-4996-b210-d554e3b38833",
                                                "sense_id": "6d651a00-ad1e-3d03-8f49-aec89d6754ff",
                                                "text": "A strikingly beautiful bird, the quetzal is the national emblem of Guatemala, appearing on its currency and postage. The quetzal ranges from southern Mexico to Costa Rica."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0271f589-8e24-4e64-8334-506a8d158e2d",
                                                "sense_id": "6d651a00-ad1e-3d03-8f49-aec89d6754ff",
                                                "text": "This particular wild avocado species had beautiful small black fruits set in a red cap that made it easy for the quetzals to find them."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "aec37fbe-575a-3909-8612-e2ce04576509",
                                        "entry_id": "454ea17c-26aa-3d82-ab46-a6b20b839381",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A monetary unit used in Guatemala, equal to 100 centavos."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "81b14f8c-8cb7-4ac9-a51f-c5700cc4925a",
                                                "sense_id": "aec37fbe-575a-3909-8612-e2ce04576509",
                                                "text": "In 2002 Guatemala officially declared the U.S. dollar as legal tender to circulate in parallel to the national currency, the quetzal. This is not likely to last for long as the quetzal is not widely accepted and is considered a weak store of value."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "abe4daf0-d115-403c-924f-6d9532ee8a21",
                                                "sense_id": "aec37fbe-575a-3909-8612-e2ce04576509",
                                                "text": "In this situation, they chose a policy mix of moderate monetary tightening, tight fiscal policy, and central bank intervention in the foreign exchange market to prevent excessive appreciation of the quetzal, without pursuing an exchange rate target[…]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ff688be3-2248-4ac2-bf73-e759e17f3c9f",
                                                "sense_id": "aec37fbe-575a-3909-8612-e2ce04576509",
                                                "text": "To cope with the subsequent mounting pressures on the domestic currency, the Bank of Guatemala (Banguat) started to intervene in the foreign exchange market to moderate the quetzal depreciation and tightened monetary policy."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4698f276-9164-4f44-9253-ab5ef92aa52d",
                        "source_entry_id": "0038713c-bc12-368b-8759-18a29e7c9169",
                        "source_sense_description": "oiseau",
                        "target_lang_word": "quetzal",
                        "target_lang_code": "es",
